      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the volume of each cube and then find the ratio of the volume of the smaller cube (with an edge length of six inches) to the volume of the larger cube (with an edge length of one foot).\n\n1. First, we need to calculate the volume of each cube. The volume \\( V \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is given by the formula \\( V = s^3 \\).\n\n2. For the smaller cube with edge length of six inches:\n   \\[\n   V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. For the larger cube with edge length of one foot:\n   \\[\n   V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. The ratio of the volume of the smaller cube to the volume of the larger cube is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n   \\]\n\n5. To simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{216}{1728}\\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. The GCD of 216 and 1728 is 216. Therefore, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 216:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code:\n```python\nfrom math import gcd\n\n# Edge lengths in inches\nsmall_cube_edge = 6\nlarge_cube_edge = 12\n\n# Volume calculation\nsmall_cube_volume = small_cube_edge ** 3\nlarge_cube_volume = large_cube_edge ** 3\n\n# Ratio of the volumes\nratio = small_cube_volume / large_cube_volume\n\n# Simplify the ratio to a common fraction\ncommon_divisor = gcd(small_cube_volume, large_cube_volume)\nsimplified_ratio = (small_cube_volume // common_divisor, large_cube_volume // common_divisor)\n\nprint(simplified_ratio)\n```\n```output\n(1, 8)\n```\nThe ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\).",
